BY021 [*] `@property` can be written as `var name` with accessors
  --> BY021.by:46:5
   |
44 |   class Widening:
45 |       # the setter's parameter would gain the getter's return type: unsafe
46 | /     @property
47 | |     def name(self) -> str:
48 | |         return self._name
49 | |
50 | |     @name.setter
51 | |     def name(self, value):
52 | |         self._name = value
   | |__________________________^
help: Replace with a `var name` declaration
   |
45 |     # the setter's parameter would gain the getter's return type: unsafe
   -     @property
   -     def name(self) -> str:
   -         return self._name
   -
   -     @name.setter
   -     def name(self, value):
   -         self._name = value
46 +     var name: str
47 +         get() = self._name
48 +         set(value):
49 +             self._name = value
50 |
   |
note: This is an unsafe fix and may change runtime behavior

BY021 [*] `@property` can be written as `let banner` with accessors
  --> BY021.by:57:5
   |
55 |   class Blocks:
56 |       # a getter that is more than a `return`
57 | /     @property
58 | |     def banner(self) -> str:
59 | |         base = self._name
60 | |         return base.upper()
   | |___________________________^
help: Replace with a `let banner` declaration
   |
56 |     # a getter that is more than a `return`
   -     @property
   -     def banner(self) -> str:
   -         base = self._name
   -         return base.upper()
57 +     let banner: str
58 +         get():
59 +             base = self._name
60 +             return base.upper()
61 |
   |

